# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is gitignored. Everything here is OPTIONAL —
# the engine is LOCAL-FIRST and works with zero config (see engine/models.py):
#   - the Story brain defaults to `auto`: it uses your local Ollama (auto-picking the
#     best installed model, prefer qwen3 > qwen2.5 > llama3.1 > gemma3 …) when Ollama
#     is running, else the deterministic offline TEMPLATE. It NEVER reaches for paid cloud.
#   - the drawing fallback defaults to `off`: recipes + composition + the Tabler catalog
#     cover ~98% of concepts; the rest become an instant labeled box (no slow LLM-SVG).
# So: install Ollama + `ollama pull qwen3:4b` (or qwen2.5:7b) and real lessons just work.

# --- Story brain: auto (default) | template | ollama | gemini --------------------
# `auto` already prefers local Ollama; set `template` to force offline, `ollama` to
# require it (warns if down). Force a specific model with OLLAMA_STORY_MODEL.
# STORY_PROVIDER=auto
# OLLAMA_STORY_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# --- Drawing fallback: off (default) | fixture | ollama | gemini ------------------
# Leave off unless you really want on-the-fly LLM-SVG for long-tail concepts.
# ENGINE_SVG_PROVIDER=off
# OLLAMA_SVG_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# --- Ollama host ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# --- Cloud (OPT-IN ONLY — never a default; keep keys OUT of source) ---------------
# Set BOTH to use Gemini for a job; prefer a real secrets manager over this file.
# STORY_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Legacy v1/v2 lanes (offline mp4 + v2 action board) ---------------------------
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b
# OLLAMA_LESSON_MODEL=gemma3:4b

# --- Server (read by the Makefile) ------------------------------------------------
# PORT=8000
# HOST=127.0.0.1
